# Dummy .cursorrules for testing

## General
- Always respond in a concise, professional tone.
- Prefer small, focused changes over large refactors.
- Never modify files outside the scope of the request.

## Code style
- Use 4-space indentation for Python and 2-space indentation for JavaScript/TypeScript.
- Add type hints to all new Python functions.
- Name variables descriptively; avoid single-letter names except loop counters.

## Testing
- Every new function must have at least one unit test.
- Do not delete or skip existing tests to make a build pass.

## Security
- Never hardcode secrets, API keys, or tokens.
- Validate and sanitize all external input.

## Documentation
- Add a docstring to every public function.
- Update README.md when behavior changes.
